# 밥친구 — shared storage
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the two values from the Supabase
# dashboard (Project Settings → API). With both set, tables are shared between
# devices; with either missing the app falls back to localStorage and keeps
# working on one device, so a developer without keys can still run everything.
#
# The anon key is designed to be public and ships inside the browser bundle.
# That is safe *because* row level security is enabled in supabase/schema.sql —
# run that file before pointing the app at a new project, or the key becomes a
# licence for anyone to delete the pilot's tables.
#
# Which key is which, because the dashboard renamed them and the new names do
# not look like keys at all:
#
#   sb_publishable_…   the public one. This is what goes below.
#   sb_secret_…        bypasses row level security completely. Never here.
#                      Anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the browser
#                      bundle, so putting the secret key below would hand every
#                      visitor the ability to delete the pilot's tables.
#
# Older projects issue JWT-shaped keys beginning `eyJ` instead; the anon one is
# still the public one and the service_role one is still the dangerous one.
#
# The URL is the project address — https://<ref>.supabase.co — not a key. They
# sit next to each other in the dashboard and are easy to swap.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── 서울관광재단 음식관광 데이터베이스 ────────────────────────────────
#
# data.go.kr dataset 15097605, served from seoul.openapi.redtable.global.
# Free, no usage restriction. Optional: without it the app builds and runs
# exactly as before, because this data is read at build time and committed.
#
# Note what is missing from the name: no VITE_ prefix. Vite exposes only
# VITE_* to the browser, so the prefix is what decides whether a key ships
# to every visitor. This one must not, and the naming is the guarantee
# rather than a note somebody has to remember.
#
# Used by `npm run seoul-food` — see scripts/seoul-food-api.mjs for why this
# API cannot be called from the app at runtime (no id filter, 1,000 rows a
# page, 168 pages for the restaurant list alone).
SEOUL_FOOD_API_KEY=
